    "body": "When `sp_min_token_num` is unset, vLLM auto-computes an SP threshold via `get_sequence_parallelism_threshold()`. For small models (e.g. `hmellor/tiny-random-LlamaForCausalLM`) or dummy-loaded models with overridden `hidden_size`, this returns `None` (below `SP_MIN_HIDDEN_SIZE`), silently disabling SP — meaning the correctness tests weren't actually exercising SP or AsyncTP paths.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`test_sequence_parallel.py`**: Add `\"sp_min_token_num\": 0` to `pass_config` in `_compare_sp()` to force SP enabled regardless of model size.\n- **`test_async_tp.py`**: Add `\"sp_min_token_num\": 0` to `pass_config` in `test_async_tp_pass_correctness()` — AsyncTP internally requires SP, same silent-disable risk applies.\n\nConsistent with the existing pattern in `tests/compile/fusions_e2e/test_tp2_async_tp.py` which already sets `sp_min_token_num=512` for the same reason. Using `0` is more aggressive: SP applies at any batch size.\n\n```python\ncompilation_config = {\n    \"mode\": CompilationMode.VLLM_COMPILE,\n    \"compile_sizes\": [4, 8],\n    \"pass_config\": {\n        \"enable_sp\": True,\n        \"fuse_gemm_comms\": fuse_gemm_comms,\n        # Override threshold to ensure SP is applied even for small models.\n        \"sp_min_token_num\": 0,\n    },\n}\n```\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n⚡ Quickly spin up Copilot coding agent tasks from anywhere on your macOS or Windows machine with [Raycast](https://gh.io/cca-raycast-docs).\n",
